---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LINKS, PROJECT_CARDS } from '../components/siteConfig';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CV — James Huson | Applied AI Systems Engineer"
  description="Applied AI systems engineer building auditable agent workflows, governed runtimes, and production delivery systems."
  active="cv"
>
  <div class="kicker">James Huson · Applied AI Systems Engineer</div>
  <h1 class="h1">I build the systems around the model.</h1>

  <div class="headshot">
    <a href={LINKS.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" title="Open LinkedIn">
      <img src="/assets/James-Headshot.jpg" alt="James — Headshot" loading="eager" />
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="sub">
    I design and ship applied AI systems that connect models to real workflows while preserving
    deterministic validation, security boundaries, auditability, and operational control. My work
    spans agent orchestration, governed tool execution, developer infrastructure, and production
    delivery.
  </p>

  <div class="btnrow">
    <a class="btn primary" href={LINKS.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
      >Contact me on LinkedIn</a
    >
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects">View Projects</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/lab">Open the Lab</a>
  </div>

  <section class="card" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2>Positioning</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">
      Applied AI platform and systems engineering across TypeScript, Node.js, Python, PostgreSQL,
      CI/CD, cloud deployment, schema-gated workflows, agent tooling, threat modeling, and
      operational verification. I am strongest where architecture, implementation, and commercial
      constraints have to agree.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>Applied AI systems:</strong> design agent workflows, tool boundaries, context flows,
          validation paths, deterministic fallbacks, and audit surfaces.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Platform delivery:</strong> TypeScript strict, Node, Python, PostgreSQL, Astro, Nginx,
          GitHub, DigitalOcean, Cloudflare, CI/CD, and boring deploy discipline.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Architecture judgment:</strong> frame the problem, lock constraints, define boundaries,
          choose the smallest useful build path, and make trade-offs explicit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Engineering governance:</strong> schema gates, prompt/version discipline, threat tests,
          provenance, human review, and reproducible delivery around model output.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="pillrow">
        <span class="pill">TypeScript</span><span class="pill">Node</span>
        <span class="pill">Nginx</span><span class="pill">Astro</span>
        <span class="pill">DigitalOcean</span><span class="pill">Cloudflare</span>
        <span class="pill">Python</span><span class="pill">PostgreSQL</span>
        <span class="pill">Agent systems</span><span class="pill">AI governance</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Operating principles</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>Start with the problem, the constraints, and the economics—not the tooling.</li>
        <li>
          Prefer static-first, composable systems over heavy stacks with unclear operating cost.
        </li>
        <li>Make deployment boring, rollback cheap, and provenance visible.</li>
        <li>
          Prototype fast, then harden deliberately when the design proves it deserves to live.
        </li>
        <li>Use AI aggressively, but keep authority, judgment, and accountability human.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top:12px">
        ExNulla is the reference implementation of how I work: deliberate scope, visible proof,
        repeatable delivery, and a bias toward systems that survive contact with reality.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>
        <strong>Operator background:</strong> I spent 20+ years designing and building businesses, operations,
        and revenue systems before formalizing that experience in software and AI systems.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Working style:</strong> I define the problem, design the system, build the assets, test
        the weak points, and improve what breaks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>ExNulla:</strong> a public engineering portfolio and live reference system spanning architecture,
        repositories, CI/CD, infrastructure, demos, and documentation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Proof:</strong> the work is documented, shipped, inspectable, and increasingly open-source.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">
      The result is a technical portfolio that can be inspected instead of taken on faith.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Range</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>Software / infra:</strong> TypeScript strict, JavaScript, Node.js, Astro, Vite, Nginx,
          Git/GitHub, PostgreSQL basics, SQLite, GraphQL exposure, Rust in active learning, Docker-aware
          CI/provenance thinking.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloud / delivery:</strong> DigitalOcean, Cloudflare, Vercel, static deploy architecture,
          artifact isolation, version stamping, CI/CD hygiene.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Creative / tooling:</strong> Blender, SketchUp, 3D CAD, Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve,
          documentation systems, spreadsheet and financial workflow tooling.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI stack:</strong> LLM application architecture, agent workflows, prompt/version control,
          schema-gated outputs, tool integration, evaluation, and deterministic multi-agent build workflows.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>What I am optimizing for</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>Target roles:</strong> Applied AI Engineer, AI Platform Engineer, AI Solutions Architect,
          Agent Infrastructure Engineer, Forward-Deployed AI Engineer, or Staff Software Engineer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Value to a team:</strong> bridge product, operations, business constraints, security,
          and implementation without losing the thread between architecture and delivery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>My edge:</strong> I think in systems that must be built, operated, explained, and made
          economically viable.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top:12px">
        I am strongest where architecture, execution, and commercial reality all have to agree.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section>
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px">Case studies (curated)</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      {
        PROJECT_CARDS.slice(0, 6).map((p) => (
          <article class="card">
            <h2 style="font-size:16px; margin:0 0 8px">{p.title}</h2>
            <p class="small" style="margin:0">
              {p.outcome}
            </p>
            <div class="pillrow">
              {p.tags.map((t) => (
                <span class="pill">{t}</span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="btnrow">
              <a class="btn ghost" href={p.href}>
                Open
              </a>
              {p.repo ? (
                <a class="btn ghost" href={p.repo} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                  Repo
                </a>
              ) : null}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .headshot {
      margin-top: 16px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 14px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .headshot img {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
      border-radius: 18px;
      object-fit: cover;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: var(--card);
    }
    .headshot a {
      display: inline-flex;
      border-radius: 18px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .headshot a:hover img {
      border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 60%, var(--fg));
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    }
    .headshot a:hover img {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
